+## Static web root
+
+`StaticRoot.file(root: Path, rendered: String): Option[Path]` is the one containment check of Chronicle's and Haystack's
+static routes: the root's real path is resolved on every call, one leading `/` is stripped from the rendered URL path
+(`index.html` for the empty rest), and the normalized candidate is returned only when it lies under the real root, is a
+regular file, and its own real path lies under the real root too (a symbolic link inside the root may not leave it). It
+blocks, decodes nothing and throws a failing real-path lookup (an absent root included); status, headers and caching
+belong to the calling HTTP adapter.
+
 ## distage / pinned Cats IO
 
 `CatsIOInjector.apply(): izumi.distage.model.Injector[IO]` is the shared distage
